# Rust build output
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Build results on 'Bin' directories (Visual Studio template convention)
**/[Bb]in/*
# ...but NOT Cargo's `src/bin/` convention.
#
# ⚠ This negation is load-bearing and is carried over from noetl/ehdb, where its
# absence broke CI. The rule above matches `src/bin/*.rs`, so a bin target's
# source is silently excluded: the crate builds locally because the file is on
# disk, `git add` skips it without a word, and `git status` never shows it
# because ignored files are not listed. A clean checkout is the first place it
# can be seen. `tests/target_hygiene.rs` guards the same class.
!**/src/[Bb]in/*

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
